id: pm-he6i
title: "Correct the closeout record: the upstream template SDK defect is mitigated, not fixed"
description: "Tracks gh:unbraind/pm-presets#184 (filed 2026-10-31, missed by the blind issue watch). The closeout of the upstream-template-defect item marked it delivered with PR #170 and listed it under CHANGELOG 'Fixed', but PR #170 only ships the package's fail-closed adapter mitigation: the host defects remain on upstream main (parseStoredTemplateOptions still assigns arbitrary accepted keys by indexed assignment into normalized, builtinTemplateDocument still indexes BUILTIN_TEMPLATES without an own-property check, and resolveTypeSynonym still indexes the ordinary-object synonym table — re-verified on upstream main 2026-11-02). The canonical item itself says the upstream follow-up stays open and requires host SDK/CLI own-key regression coverage before revisiting those refusals. Action: record a follow-up here that keeps the upstream fix open (watch upstream releases for own-key checks in template parsing and type synonyms), and correct the CHANGELOG wording from 'Fixed' to 'Mitigated (package-side)' so consumers do not read the host defect as repaired."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: closeout,"gh:unbraind/pm-presets#184","gh:unbraind/pm-presets#203"
created_at: "2026-11-02T09:18:08.631Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-09T11:11:57.451Z"
author: pi-glm
comments[22]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T12:40:00.601Z",codex-sol,"Main still attributes the upstream defect to adapter PR 170. Plan: append a status correction preserving all native history, retain compatibility refusals, and add a real nongit SDK tracker regression that checks unresolved upstream work cannot be emitted as Fixed by the closeout workflow."
  "2026-11-06T12:44:20.929Z",codex-sol,"Failing-first reproduction: the canonical tracker copied to a nongit scratch tracker and read with PmClient reports pm-7km8 closed instead of open; generated Fixed notes include its host-defect title. The correction appends native history, clears completion/resolution fields and keeps the host follow-up open. A generic upstream:unresolved gate will reject done-role closure before closeout changelog generation."
  "2026-11-06T12:48:01.617Z",codex-sol,"The pinned changelog generator deliberately restores closed snapshots from immutable release tags, so reopening alone does not remove the old Fixed claim. All package/release generator invocations now exclude upstream-tagged follow-ups: these are foreign implementation work, not package fixes. Package mitigation/correction items remain eligible. The explicit upstream:unresolved marker separately guards automatic completion; no tagged snapshots or existing audit records are edited. The first native reopen attempt rejected unsupported timestamp unsets without changing state; the supported status transition cleared completion fields automatically."
  "2026-11-06T12:52:45.093Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral reverts in a disposable copy all fail as intended: restoring the original upstream item fails closed-versus-open; removing verifyCloseoutAttribution enforcement fails the real SDK fixture's expected finding; removing generator upstream exclusion fails the invocation contract. Restoring all three passes 3/3. Native status roles (including a custom terminal_done alias) and real CLI gate exit are covered. No reviewed-checkout files were mutated for these proofs."
  "2026-11-06T13:02:38.694Z",codex-sol,"Local verification passes: 37/37 closeout/workflow/changelog-date regressions, and the combined diff/closeout focus passes 11/11 with no skips. Compiler lint, typecheck, test compilation and complete docstrings pass. Native histories remain prefix extensions of main, and the generated changelog removes only the false upstream Fixed section while retaining the adapter feature entry. Full release gates will run in PR CI."
  "2026-11-06T13:06:55.169Z",codex-sol,"Implementation and three revert proofs are complete; the upstream follow-up stays open and unclaimed. Isolated-home strict tracker health passes with append-only histories and the corrected generated changelog. PR CI and bot review are the remaining external checks. Releasing this implementation claim, leaving status in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-06T14:08:10.865Z",codex-sol,"Review round 1 on PR 203 found a possible closeout compatibility regression: the new guarded hook may lose historical-only generation when the package version is untagged. All current-head CI gates are green, including 348/348 tests in each npm/Bun full release gate and both Node matrix jobs. Reproducing the untagged-version scenario against the pinned generator before choosing a fix; no review finding is accepted without evidence."
  "2026-11-06T14:28:21.805Z",codex-sol,"Confirmed review finding PRRT_kwDOSp_1PM60iOzn with a real SDK tracker and disposable Git history: an untagged package version fails closeout with MISSING_REQUESTED_RELEASE. The hook now explicitly suppresses pending-release generation. CI delegates exact-byte checks to the pinned generator in either legitimate historical or prepared-release mode. Publication additionally requires the original strict release checker via prepublishOnly; actual release workflow generation/check semantics remain strict. The regression accepts historical closeouts, rejects them for publication, accepts prepared release notes, and rejects corrupted artifacts without rewriting them."
  "2026-11-06T14:41:03.068Z",codex-sol,"Round 1 fix verified: reverting only the closeout no-pending-release flag fails with MISSING_REQUESTED_RELEASE; reverting only historical checker support fails the CI check on the valid historical artifact. Restoring both passes. Final linked real-SDK/Git fixture tests pass 4/4, workflow/date regressions pass 34/34, and lint/typecheck/test compilation/docstrings pass. The fixture uses fixed historical completion/tag timestamps, explicit synthetic Git identity, and scrubbed credential/Git-routing variables. Prepared release notes pass the strict publisher check; historical-only and corrupted notes are refused. No publication or target-repository tags were created. The previously pushed head passed all CI, but this code fix requires fresh exact-head CI and re-review. Releasing the claim pending those checks."
  "2026-11-06T17:43:02.424Z",codex-sol,"Resumed for CodeRabbit round 2. Confirmed the tracker-copy filter incorrectly examines absolute ancestors: an excluded parent segment can skip the entire source. Add a failing real-SDK nongit regression covering every excluded parent name, retained tracker data and relative exclusions, then scope the shared fixture copy filter to the source root. Existing issue fixes and completed gate receipts remain unchanged. GitHub GraphQL quota currently blocks pr-state; REST supplied the full review body and finding."
  "2026-11-06T17:47:36.508Z",codex-sol,"Round 2 regression first failed because an excluded locks ancestor skipped the whole tracker. Shared copyTracker now filters relative to its absolute source root and matches complete segments at the path start or after a separator. The real SDK regression exercises all five excluded parent names, top-level and nested exclusions, similarly named retained directories, unchanged settings/item/history bytes and complete nongit copied-tracker reads. Two disposable behavioral reverts independently fail: restoring absolute-path matching skips the root; removing the first-segment boundary retains excluded runtime data. Restoring the helper passes. Lint, typecheck, test compilation and docstrings pass. An initial combined run hit the existing history subprocess timeout; a serial rerun is pending without changing any timeout or threshold."
  "2026-11-06T17:51:34.807Z",codex-sol,"Round 2 validation complete: the serial closeout/history command passes 5/5 with no skips, both directly and through pm test --run --only-last --progress. The initial concurrent local run hit the unchanged history subprocess timeout; serial execution passes without relaxing it. Both isolated filter reverts fail and restoration passes. Lint, typecheck, test compilation, docstrings and append-only history-prefix verification pass. Ready to commit the test-only correction together with this native tracker evidence; fresh exact-head CI and queued full review follow the push."
  "2026-11-07T01:17:58.202Z",codex-agent,"Review round: fetched every review thread and all comments; one unresolved Windows npm launcher finding (PRRT_kwDOSp_1PM60sUkZ). Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Remote branch includes current main. Reuse only validated launcher and regression hunks from saved WIP; exclude local artifacts. Verify the whole PR for related platform-launch defects, record behavioral reverts, and run unchanged targeted and release gates before push."
  "2026-11-07T01:20:05.897Z",codex-agent,"Validated PRRT_kwDOSp_1PM60sUkZ: closeout history now uses the shared launcher, selecting npm.cmd with shell execution only for Windows npm while preserving direct Git/Node execution elsewhere. Reused only the saved-WIP launcher/history/Windows-CI hunks, added portable real-process regressions and ignored .local. Whole-PR review found no further instance: other new child processes use process.execPath; existing npx coverage spawning already enables the Windows shell. Targeted suite: 8 passed, 0 failed, 1 Windows-only skip. Disposable-copy behavioral reverts independently restore legacy direct spawning, remove npm.cmd selection, or remove shell execution: each fails the regression; restoring the fixed helper passes 2/2 after each mutation. Actual Windows npm.cmd/parser acceptance is delegated to the Windows CI job, which now also runs the complete closeout-history regression."
  "2026-11-07T01:23:22.744Z",codex-agent,"Linked targeted test run passes (8 executed tests, 0 failures, 1 intentional Windows-only skip). Typecheck, lint and test compilation pass. All changed history streams retain main as a byte-identical prefix; the coverage item history is new on this branch. Fresh build leaves committed dist unchanged. Strict CI-style tracker health passes all 10 checks with an advisory telemetry queue notice. Default-environment health instead reports an ambient global pm-github host-version skew (pinned host 2026.11.2 versus extension install host 2026.11.6); no package dependency or global installation was changed. Full npm and Bun release checks use isolated HOME and stripped credentials, sequentially with at most two test workers."
  "2026-11-07T01:27:25.395Z",codex-agent,"Full npm run release:check passes in 352 seconds with isolated HOME and credential-free child environment: 352 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped, 100% lines/branches/functions across all 36 configured gated sources. Also passes typecheck, lint, 102-file/228-declaration docstring coverage, production audit, package dry run, closeout attribution, canonical changelog, publication attestation and version-derived changelog dates. Committed dist matches the build. Full Bun release gate is running sequentially at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-11-07T01:34:21.934Z",codex-agent,"Final review-round result: full npm and Bun release:check both pass at unchanged thresholds (npm 352 seconds; Bun 415 seconds). Each executes 352/352 tests with 0 failures and 0 skips and measures 100% lines, branches and functions across all 36 configured gated sources; docstrings cover 102 files and 228 declarations. Typecheck, lint, test compilation, build, audit, package dry run, closeout attribution, changelog, publish-attestation and changelog-date checks pass. Targeted and linked PM runs each pass 8 tests with 1 intentional Windows-only skip. Three independently failing helper reverts and passing 2/2 restorations are recorded above. Native Windows npm launch/revert and full history acceptance are configured in Windows CI and remain pending the pushed head. No finding was refused; no other valid instance found in the whole PR. No threshold, dependency pin or product source changed this round. Release my claim while leaving the item in progress for orchestrator verification; regenerate changelog after this final tracker write, verify final commit identity/privacy and history-prefix integrity, then push only the PR branch and delete its saved local WIP branch."
  "2026-11-09T10:46:34.466Z",codex-agent,"Continuation inspected existing branch, PR 203, all review-thread comments and tracker evidence without reading raw agent transcripts. Remote head already includes main and no unresolved review threads remain. Latest review scope request is satisfied by the existing direct link to issue 184. Windows CI still fails on the null-device Git config; replace every Git/npm config null-device path with a real empty temporary file, add behavioral regressions, verify unchanged full npm/Bun gates and native Windows CI."
  "2026-11-09T10:49:18.814Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed Windows failure in job 128536469508: Git rejects the null-device global config path. Replaced every package Git/npm config null-device with the shared ordinary empty-file helper, scoped to caller cleanup; the audit also strips inherited credentials and preserves status. Whole-PR review found no other null-device config use. Targeted suite passes 10 tests with 1 intentional Windows-only skip; docstrings pass for 111 files and 241 declarations. Two isolated behavioral reverts fail: returning the null device from the shared helper fails both config regressions; routing only audit config back to the null device fails its process regression. Each restoration passes 2/2. Real Git/npm reads and fake-audit processes cover paths with spaces, exact audit arguments, both exit outcomes and cleanup. Windows CI now runs these same portable regressions alongside the complete history fixture."
  "2026-11-09T10:58:58.158Z",codex-agent,"Full npm run release:check passes with isolated HOME, ordinary empty Git/npm config and stripped credential variables: 367/367 tests, no failures or skips, 512.6 seconds. Coverage remains 100% lines, branches and functions across the unchanged 36-source scope; typecheck, lint, build/test compilation, docstrings (111 files, 241 declarations), production audit, package inspection, attribution, canonical changelog, publish attestation and changelog-date checks pass. Strict tracker health passes 10/10 and histories preserve main prefixes. Existing maintainer-authored merge 67271ad remains intact and passes the repository identity audit; the author range therefore includes that earlier merge in addition to bot commits. New continuation commits use the required SteveBot identity. Bun release validation will run sequentially."
  "2026-11-09T11:10:44.364Z",codex-agent,"Native Windows job 129119826883 validates the ordinary empty Git/npm config and audit regressions (both pass), then exposes a second pre-existing launch defect: explicit --pm-bin ./node_modules/.bin/pm cannot run the POSIX host shim. The pinned pm-changelog already resolves its installed host through the package manifest and current Node executable when --pm-bin is omitted. Removed that override consistently from package generation/check scripts, release workflow calls and the changelog-date probe. The real history fixture now provides only the pinned packages and an unusable pm shim; an isolated behavioral revert restoring the explicit shim fails the real changelog read, and restoration passes 1/1. Final focused launcher/history/config/workflow/date tests pass 41 with 1 intentional Windows-only skip; test compilation, typecheck, lint and 111-file/241-declaration docstrings pass. Full npm and Bun gates on the initial config-fix code each pass 367/367 with no skips (512.6 and 570.9 seconds). Fresh exact-head CI will certify the additional host-launch correction; no dependency pin or threshold changed."
  "2026-11-09T11:11:52.525Z",codex-agent,"Pre-push closeout for this continuation: all three current behavioral reverts are recorded above (shared null-device helper, audit-only null-device routing, explicit POSIX pm shim); restored regressions pass. Final targeted and linked PM runs pass 41 tests with 1 intentional Windows-only skip. Full local npm and Bun release gates pass 367/367 on the config-fix commit; the subsequent host-launch correction passes its focused workflow/date/history checks and will receive fresh complete npm/Bun CI. Previous native Windows run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-presets/actions/runs/42605350120 confirmed both config regressions and exposed the now-corrected host shim issue. Final check status is available at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-presets/pull/203/checks; allow the final push to generate a fresh exact-head run. No unresolved review threads or outside-diff findings remain; issue 184 is directly linked. Package thresholds and dependency pins are unchanged, committed dist is unchanged, and the upstream repair item remains open. Release this claim without closing the item; final tracker writes precede CI verification."
